content.text:
Day part is 40px wide. At 320, instead of hiding whole day, we can show day only:
```
@media max 340:
.day-readout { display:flex; }? 
.day-readout .readout-part:first-child { display:flex; }
.day-readout .readout-part:last-child { display:none; }
```
But earlier at max 760, `.readout-part:first-child { display:none; }`; override to flex at 340. Set grid to `1fr auto auto` (brand, day, tools). Tools 125, day maybe 50, brand 77, gaps + padding = 77+50+125+16+22=290 <305. Good. Keep day pill border. Let's update 340 block:
```
.topbar { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto auto; }
.day-readout { display: flex; }
.day-readout .readout-part:first-child { display:flex; }
.day-readout .readout-part:last-child { display:none; }
```
But the base `.day-readout` display:flex; hide was display:none. Override to flex. Then day visible. Note max 760 first child display none; override later in cascade with equal specificity? `.day-readout .readout-part:first-child` specificity (0,2,1) same; later 340 block wins. Good.

Test 320 width.

